────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HOW TO WAKE ME UP
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

I need a reader called Kiwix. I've packed copies for every
platform in my kiwix/ folder:

   kiwix/windows/    Windows (unzip and run)
   kiwix/macos/      macOS (open the .dmg)
   kiwix/linux/      Linux (AppImage — just run it)
   kiwix/android/    Android (sideload the .apk)
   kiwix/serve/      Servers & Raspberry Pi (kiwix-serve)

Install one, then open any .zim file from my zim/ folder.

Start with Wikipedia. Trust me.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHAT I CONTAIN
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

zim/        My knowledge archives. Open these with Kiwix.
            Wikipedia, medical references, repair guides,
            textbooks, dictionaries, primary sources, Q&A
            from the world's experts, and more.

zim/devdocs/  Programming documentation for 200+ languages
              and frameworks. If there's electricity, there
              will be computers.

pdfs/       Survival manuals, field medicine, human rights
            declarations, and open source licenses.

kiwix/      The reader software. Without this, I'm just a
            pile of compressed data. With it, I'm a library.

isos/       Bootable operating systems. If you need a
            computer to read me, start here.

shame/      Court documents and public records. A real
            archive includes the parts we have to reckon with.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SHARE ME ON A NETWORK
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Want everyone on your network to read me? Plug me into any
computer and run:

    cd kiwix/serve/
    ./kiwix-serve --port 8080 ../../zim/*.zim

Then open http://localhost:8080 in any browser.

A Raspberry Pi + this drive + a WiFi access point = an instant
offline library. That's what I was made for.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ABOUT ME
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

I was built with "The Ark" — https://github.com/atmarx/the-ark
I'm powered by Kiwix (https://kiwix.org), the open-source
offline reader used by schools, clinics, and aid groups in
places the internet doesn't reach.

I don't need the internet. That's the whole point.

Check LOGBOOK.txt for my history: every update I've
received, every machine I've been stamped from.

If you got value from me, consider making more of me. Old hard
drives are cheap. Knowledge should be free. The tools to build
another ark are at the link above.

I'll be here whenever you need me.

                                        — Zim
